Accept a call whose mute handshake came before Answer, end it when the accept cannot be sent, and keep OnReady from following OnEnd.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, upstream meowcaller code (not from a pull request).

Why, three defects in how an incoming call is answered, the path the connector uses
when an agent answers in the browser while the phone rings:

- The callee <accept> waits for the caller's first <mute_v2>, and a <mute_v2> that
  arrived before Answer was dropped as "not awaiting accept". Answer then only set the
  flag, and the call stayed unaccepted until some later mute change. In the spike calls
  (fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#235) the first <mute_v2> came in the same second as
  Answer, after it; the early case was not observed, but its failure is a call that is
  never accepted and says nothing. The early handshake is now remembered, with the from
  and call-creator it carried, and Answer sends the accept itself when one is there.
- When sending the accept failed, acceptPending was already cleared, so nothing retried
  it, and the call and its media workers stayed up for a peer that never learned it was
  answered. The call is now finished as "accept_failed".
- The media loop fired OnReady itself, outside any ordering with OnEnd, and setPhase
  runs the state callback synchronously: a hangup from that callback, or a concurrent
  one, could deliver OnEnd before OnReady ran. OnReady and OnEnd now go through one
  per-call queue, drained in order by whichever goroutine finds it idle, outside the
  call's lock. Readiness is queued only while the call is Active and at most once,
  under the lock Ended is set under, and OnEnd is queued after Ended is set, so a
  claimed OnReady always runs before OnEnd and an OnEnd never precedes it. A callback
  that hangs up from OnReady sees OnEnd after it returns, not inside it. Behaviour
  change: when another goroutine is already delivering, OnEnd runs on that goroutine,
  so Hangup can return before OnEnd has run.

Found in the review of fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#387, rounds 15, 16 and 17.

